export const LICENSE_THIRD_PARTY = "WunderPaint — Third-Party Licenses\n======================================\n\nWunderPaint is licensed under the GNU General Public License,\nversion 2 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later); see license.txt for the full text.\n\nThis file lists the third-party components that are BUNDLED with and\ndistributed as part of the plugin, together with their licenses and\ncopyright/attribution notices. Every component is under a license that is\ncompatible with the GPL.\n\nA note on Apache-2.0 components: the Apache License 2.0 is compatible with\nGPL version 3 but not with GPL version 2 on its own. Because this plugin is\nlicensed as \"GPL-2.0-OR-LATER\", the \"or later\" option permits GPLv3, under\nwhich the Apache-2.0 components below may be combined and redistributed.\n\n\nBundled JavaScript libraries\n----------------------------\n\nag-psd — PSD read/write\n  MIT License. Copyright (c) 2016 Agamnentzar.\n\ngifenc — animated GIF encoding\n  MIT License. Copyright (c) 2017 Matt DesLauriers.\n\njszip — ZIP reading/writing (project files, exports)\n  Dual-licensed MIT or GPL-3.0-or-later; used here under the MIT License.\n  Copyright (c) 2009-2016 Stuart Knightley, David Duponchel, Franz Buchinger,\n  António Afonso. Includes pako (MIT AND Zlib, Copyright (C) 2014-2017 Vitaly\n  Puzrin and Andrei Tuputcyn), lie (MIT, Copyright (c) 2014-2018 Calvin\n  Metcalf, Jordan Harband), readable-stream (MIT, Copyright Node.js\n  contributors) and setimmediate (MIT, Copyright (c) 2012 Barnesandnoble.com).\n\nonnxruntime-web — local (in-browser) neural-network inference\n  MIT License. Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. The CPU WebAssembly\n  pair ships inside the plugin under assets/ort/ (since v1.316.0). The distributed WebAssembly\n  build includes: flatbuffers (Apache-2.0, Copyright Google Inc.), long\n  (Apache-2.0, Copyright Daniel Wirtz), protobufjs (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c)\n  2016 Daniel Wirtz), guid-typescript (ISC), platform (MIT, Copyright\n  2014-2020 Benjamin Tan) and onnxruntime-common (MIT, Microsoft Corporation).\n\n@huggingface/transformers (transformers.js) — in-browser runtime for the local\nAI features (Smart Select, Depth Blur, Blur Faces, local alt text, semantic\nimage search)\n  Apache License 2.0. Copyright Hugging Face and the transformers.js\n  contributors; the library was previously published as @xenova/transformers.\n  Bundled from npm into build/ by webpack since v1.316.0 - nothing is fetched\n  from a CDN. Its CPU ONNX-runtime WebAssembly ships alongside it in\n  assets/ort/ (Microsoft Corporation, MIT, with the Apache-2.0/BSD-3-Clause\n  components noted under onnxruntime-web above). The full Apache-2.0 text is\n  in node_modules/@huggingface/transformers/LICENSE.\n\n\nvtracer-wasm — colour image vectorization (the Vectorize command)\n  MIT License. Copyright (c) 2025 jsscheller. A WebAssembly build of VTracer\n  (https://github.com/visioncortex/vtracer, MIT, Copyright (c) 2020 Vision\n  Cortex). Ships as build/*.wasm.\n\nimagetracerjs — vectorization fallback where WebAssembly is unavailable\n  The Unlicense (public domain). By Andras Jankovics.\n\nqrcode — QR-code generation\n  MIT License. Copyright (c) 2012 Ryan Day. Includes dijkstrajs (MIT) and\n  pngjs (MIT, Copyright (c) 2015 Luke Page & original contributors).\n\nupng-js — APNG encoding\n  MIT License. Copyright (c) 2017 Photopea.\n\n\nBundled build-time assets (embedded into the plugin build)\n----------------------------------------------------------\n\nTabler Icons — user-interface icon paths\n  MIT License. Copyright (c) 2020-present Paweł Kuna.\n  Used for the icon library chunk (src/icons-lib) and, since v1.51, for\n  curated editor UI icons (assets/ui-icons -> src/ui-icons.json).\n\nunicode-emoji-json — emoji metadata\n  MIT License. Copyright (c) Mesach Harmasendro.\n\n\nBundled machine-learning model\n------------------------------\n\nU^2-Netp segmentation model (assets/models/u2netp.onnx)\n  Used for local, in-browser background removal and subject selection\n  (no image data leaves the browser). Based on U^2-Net by Xuebin Qin et al.\n  Apache License 2.0. See assets/models/NOTICE.txt for attribution and a copy\n  of the Apache-2.0 license reference. Compatible with this plugin via the\n  \"or later\" clause of GPL-2.0-or-later (see the note above).\n\n\nBundled fonts (self-hosted in assets/fonts/)\n--------------------------------------------\n\nTen families ship inside the plugin and are served from your own site:\nRoboto, Open Sans, Inter, Montserrat, Poppins, Oswald, Bebas Neue, Anton,\nPlayfair Display and Lora. The woff2 files are sourced from the @fontsource\nproject (https://fontsource.org).\n\n  License: SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (OFL-1.1) for all ten. A copy of\n  the OFL is provided in assets/fonts/OFL.txt. Copyright belongs to the\n  respective font authors (see each family's project). The OFL is directly\n  GPL-compatible.\n\nThe rest of the catalogue is not bundled. An administrator can download it\nonce to the site's own uploads folder, after which those families are served\nlocally as well, or opt into loading them from the Google Fonts CDN instead\n(Settings, Fonts). Nothing is fetched from a font CDN unless that option is\nswitched on.\n\n\nBundled inside the free extensions (bundled-extensions/)\n--------------------------------------------------------\n\nNineteen free extensions ship with the plugin. They are editor add-ons rather\nthan WordPress plugins and run entirely in the browser. Five of them carry\nthird-party code or data of their own, listed here because it travels in the\ndownload. Where a licence asks for a notice next to the file, that notice sits\nin the extension's own folder as well.\n\nhighlight.js 11.11.1 — syntax highlighting in Code Shot (the core plus thirty\nlanguage definitions)\n  BSD-3-Clause. Copyright (c) 2006 Ivan Sagalaev and other contributors.\n  https://github.com/highlightjs/highlight.js\n  Bundled into bundled-extensions/wpie-code-shot/extension.js.\n\nthree.js 0.185.1 — the WebGL renderer that folds the paper in Origami,\nincluding RoomEnvironment from three/examples/jsm\n  MIT License. Copyright (c) 2010-2025 three.js authors.\n  https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js\n  Bundled into bundled-extensions/wpie-origami/extension.js.\n\ntz-lookup 6.1.25 — offline time zone for a pair of coordinates, so Mystic\nStudio can place a chart in local time without asking a service\n  CC0-1.0 (public domain dedication). The Dark Sky Company.\n  Bundled into bundled-extensions/wpie-mystic-studio/extension.js.\n\nJetBrains Mono — the typeface Code Shot sets code in (Regular and Bold)\n  SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (OFL-1.1), directly GPL-compatible.\n  Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors,\n  https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono. Files:\n  bundled-extensions/wpie-code-shot/fonts/JetBrainsMono-Regular.woff2 and\n  -Bold.woff2, with FONT-LICENSE.md in the same folder.\n\nMoon photograph — the full disc in Mystic Studio\n  NASA/JPL, Galileo spacecraft, 7 December 1992 (PIA00405,\n  https://photojournal.jpl.nasa.gov/catalog/PIA00405). NASA imagery, public\n  domain, resized to 1200 px. File:\n  bundled-extensions/wpie-mystic-studio/textures/moon.jpg, with TEXTURES.md\n  in the same folder.\n\nStar positions and constellation figures — Star Map Posters, and the zodiac\nfigures Mystic Studio draws from the same source\n  Yale Bright Star Catalogue, public domain. The constellation lines come from\n  d3-celestial, BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2015 Olaf Frohn.\n  https://github.com/ofrohn/d3-celestial\n  Built into bundled-extensions/wpie-star-map/extension.js and\n  bundled-extensions/wpie-mystic-studio/extension.js; Star Map Posters also\n  names both on screen next to the finished poster.\n\nOldenburg map excerpt (bundled-extensions/wpie-map-studio/oldenburg.json)\n  Map Studio ships one small area of real map geometry so that the studio has\n  something to show before any map is fetched. Derived from OpenStreetMap,\n  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL),\n  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright. Map Studio carries the same credit\n  on screen whenever it draws a map.\n\n\nProvided by WordPress at runtime (NOT bundled)\n----------------------------------------------\n\nThe @wordpress/* packages (element, i18n, hooks, api-fetch, components, …) are\nprovided by WordPress itself at runtime and are not shipped in this plugin.\nWordPress and these packages are licensed under the GPL.\n\nBuild-only tooling (webpack/@wordpress/scripts, ESLint, Jest, Playwright,\nnode-canvas, @fontsource sources) is used only to build the plugin and is not\ndistributed with it.\n\nGeoNames place index (assets/geo/cities.json)\n---------------------------------------------\nDerived from GeoNames, licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0\n(CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nSource files: cities15000, alternateNamesV2 and countryInfo from\nhttps://download.geonames.org/export/dump/\n\nDerivation: cities of 15,000 inhabitants or more, reduced to their names in\nthe seven languages this editor ships in (en, de, fr, es, it, nl, pt),\ncoordinates rounded to four decimals, plus country code and population.\nRebuild with `node tools/build-gazetteer.mjs`. The source files are NOT\ndownloaded at run time; the index is built once and shipped.\n\nMap geometry is fetched at edit time through the plugin's server-side geo\nproxy from OpenFreeMap and the OpenStreetMap Overpass instances, and is\n(c) OpenStreetMap contributors under the Open Database License (ODbL),\nhttps://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright. One small excerpt does ship with the\nplugin as sample data; it is listed above under the bundled extensions.\n";

export const EXTERNAL_SERVICES = "This plugin can talk to a number of external services, each only when you use the feature it belongs to, and a service that needs an API key stays silent until you enter that key. There is no analytics, no tracking and no telemetry of its own, and it never sends your content anywhere by itself.\n\nThe complete list, with the exact data each service receives and when, is in the FAQ below: \"Which external services does this plugin use?\" The same list, in more detail, is at https://help.wp-image-editor.com/#services";
